# The places that the editorial check (checkeditorial.py) lets stand: a rule
# name, a blank and a phrase that is matched, without regard to case, in the
# 40 characters around the hit.  A line that begins with a number sign is a
# comment.  Every line says why in the comment above it.
#
# Just is the name of a field of a panel, and a value of it.
E1 Just: | Left, Right
E1 Just is Left, Right
# The Viewer shows the zoom 100% in its help line, as typed.
E6 0: 100%   arrows
# A message of the program that goes over two lines of a table cell.
E2 synonyms -  Please choose
# A note that a new Note marker is: the noun note, not the verb.
E2 note that a new Note
# A statement of what a file of an earlier version of Strata holds, so that
# the reader of such a file knows how it is read.
E3 A file of an earlier version has the single key
E3 Earlier versions of Strata kept the settings
E3 Earlier versions of Strata left the backups
E3 A document that was made by an earlier version
E3 were drawn as a diamond in an earlier version
E3 of earlier versions does not exist
E3 a backup that an earlier version left
# The same row in the tables of two panels that share a field, and the
# same sentence for two keys that put in the same character.
E13 The character is put in at the cursor like any letter
E13 When it is not a number above 0 the revision
# The message of the Highlight prompt, which two commands show.
E13 The message line says "Highlight the area
# The same message in two rows, one for each way that the checker fails.
E13 The spelling checker PROGRAM did not start
# A message of the program that ends with its own period inside the cell.
E15 The pages carry the banner and the marks.
# Too soon is a measure of a stop, not a promise.
E3 stop too soon or too late
# The names of two keys in a headline.
E10 PgUp and PgDn
# The names of the marker types and of a person, in the sentence case of a
# headline.
E10 Notes, Comments, Equations and the Library
E10 A Fourier transform
# E24: the words of a message or of a screen of a program, as it writes them
# (the programs spell the names of the commands in lower case).
E24 latex and dvipng are needed
E24 cannot start latex
E24 latex could not typeset
E24 latex took more than
E24 no temporary directory for latex
E24 latex: out of memory
E24 with the x11
E24 latex edit
E24 pdflatex or latex
# E25: the name of an extension of the typesetting system, written with a
# hyphen as its authors write it.
E25 (e-TeX)
# The word postscript with a small p is the noun that P.S. stands for in a
# letter, not the name of the page description language.
E26 enclosures and postscript
E26 and P.S.} (carbon copy, enclosures and postscr
# The status line of the program says LATEX EDIT in capital letters.
E26 LATEX EDIT
# The name of a Debian package is cups, in lower case.
E26 of the cups package
# A message of the program, quoted as the program prints it, begins with
# the name of the program latex or the word x11 of a build name.
E26 latex and dvipng are needed
E26 The program ENGINE (pdflatex or latex) did not run
E26 display with the x11
E26 Cannot start latex
E26 latex could not typeset the equation
E26 latex took more than 5 seconds
E26 No temporary directory for latex
E26 latex: out of memory
# A message of the Printer that is quoted as the program prints it: the text
# of the message is the program's, so the table shows it unchanged.
